WEBVTT

00:01:58.704 --> 00:02:01.871
can use their power to recreate the world.

00:02:01.871 --> 00:02:05.163
You’ve already bid 24 gems on the first,

00:02:05.163 --> 00:02:09.538
when you realize that your rival
has a dastardly advantage:

00:02:09.538 --> 00:02:12.621
a mirror that lets him see
what you’re bidding.

00:02:13.163 --> 00:02:16.996
He bids zero, 
and you win the first hexagon outright.

00:02:17.288 --> 00:02:22.371
What’s your strategy to win a matching
trio of hexagons before your rival?

00:02:22.371 --> 00:02:24.329
Pause here to figure it out for yourself.

00:02:24.329 --> 00:02:25.329
Answer in 3

00:02:25.329 --> 00:02:27.871
Answer in 2

00:02:27.871 --> 00:02:30.996
Answer in 1